    "@type": "Rating",
    "ratingValue": "5"
   },
   "reviewBody": "Made a huge batch of this paneer makhani and used butter and ground cashews for the richest flavor combo. I followed her recipe 98% of the way, with maybe slightly less garlic and more ginger, but left out Kasuri Methi, as mine was old and not flavorful or fragrant.  This is certainly the best recipe I\u2019ve used online. I used a good quantity of chili powder as we like the heat, and the flavors still shined through. I also cooked my onions very well so they would carmelize and become sweeter before I added tomatoes.  We have leftovers and definitely will enjoy this tomorrow. First time making using her recipe\u2026.. I will add this to my rotation because it\u2019s superb!!",
